title: Customising the GUI
tags: GUI
kind: overview
aliases: customisation customization customizing personalisation settings-files
summary: What of the GUI is yours to change — keys, look, commands, settings, how references are named — the file each lives in, and what takes effect without a restart.

Everything the GUI lets you change is a file of `~/.config/metafolder/gui/`, in the
[[configuration repository|The configuration repository]]. The shipped version of
each is installed by `metafolder-sync-config`, and an update merges the new shipped
version into yours ([[Updating the configuration]]). The GUI never writes a default
of its own: a file that is missing or malformed stops it at startup
([[No runtime fallback]]).

|!To change |!Edit |!Takes effect |
|what a key runs |`keybindings.toml`, or the settings view — [[Changing keybindings]] |at once from the settings view; `config:reload keybindings` after editing the file |
|colours, fonts, the look of a widget |`style.css` — [[Style and theming]] |`config:reload style` |
|the commands themselves: add yours, edit the shipped ones written in JavaScript |`commands.js` — [[User commands]] |`config:reload commands` |
|ports, page sizes, timings, the programs offered to open a file |`config.toml` — [[GUI configuration]] |at the next start |
|what a panel opens on: the columns of the list, the field of the tree… |`config.toml`, `[panel-defaults]` — [[GUI configuration]] |at the next start |
|how the target of a reference is named where one is typed or shown |`config.toml`, `[ref-seeds]` — [[Ref value seeds]] |at the next start |
|the words of the simplified query language |`core/query-grammar` — [[Editing the grammar]] |`config:reload grammar` |
|what a panel does, or a panel type of your own |`panel-types/` — [[Panel types]], [[Writing a panel type]] |at the next start |

[[Reloading the configuration]] says why some of these need a restart.

`config:open` opens the ''settings view'': the paths of these files, a button that
reloads the style sheet, and the keybinding editor.

